    "summary": "Mix of five sherds, four of them hand-made neolithic Nubian ones, one is a rim sherd and is well polished, wheel-made reused Christian (?) with shallow impressions at the outside. The others are quite eroded with different decoration at the outside.\nA: body sherd with dotted lines at the outside, no number.\nB: AWS 23, body sherd, dotted lines.\nC: AWS 51, X, AW 38/3j9, rim-sherd, herring bone like incised lines.\nD: AWS 5(?)34, small rim sherd with incised lines.\nE: AWS 206, E Bank near house, rim-sherd, shallow fine impressions at the outside, polished.",
